=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free models +
  projection + registration, unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.Projection.cs (pure SI→display projection),
  <Name>.Source.cs (the cache-then-network data port), <Name>.ViewModel.cs (INotifyPropertyChanged +
  IDisposable state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view). The generated prompt's idealized
  "VehicleListPage.xaml + ViewModel.cs under TeslaSync/Features/Vehicles" is mapped onto these real
  conventions; the surface registers with the W4 ShellPageFactory by route name ("Vehicles", already in
  RouteTable.cs L98: Page("Vehicles","vehicles",RouteGroup.Vehicles)).
- Self-contained port (matching the ChargingListPage precedent): the page owns its own VehicleListSource —
  the web page's three reads — (1) GET /vehicles roster spine (Operations.Vehicles.List, web useVehicles)
  cache-then-network; (2) a best-effort fan-out of GET /vehicles/{id}/state per vehicle
  (Operations.Vehicles.State, web fetchVehicleState, each wrapped try/catch → null asleep card); (3) a
  best-effort GET /pinned?type=vehicle read (web usePinned('vehicle')) that floats pinned vehicles to the
  top. The two mutations are POST /vehicles/sync (web syncMut) and DELETE /vehicles/{id} (web deleteMut)
  through VehicleListMutationsClient. No HTTP touches the view.
- SI units: rated_range / odometer are SI metres on the wire; conversion happens only at the display
  boundary via UnitConverters.DistanceFromSi / UnitFormatters.FormatDistance keyed off the live
  AppSettingsHost unit preference (web useUnits). The view never stores/computes non-SI.
- i18n: every visible literal flows through the ILocalizer facade with the web key names + verbatim English
  defaults (VehicleListPageRegistration.* constants). The Strings/*.resw catalog is auto-generated by
  apps/shared/i18n/generators/gen-i18n.ts from the shared web i18n source (keyed by English text); the
  surface resolves the web keys through the shell Localization bridge with the same fallback wording, so no
  hand-edit of the generated catalog is required (consistent with every other completed W7 page).
- The TeslaSync.App.Tests project links Microsoft.UI-free sources by explicit <Compile Include> (it
  references only App.Core + Generated, not the WinUI App project). The four new non-UI files
  (VehicleListPage.Model/Projection/Source/ViewModel.cs) were added to that link set so the headless tests
  compile against them; the WinUI .cs view is exercised by the app build only.

